# Release manifest. One file per release; never edit a published one, add a new .<n> instead.
SWIFT_VERSION=6.4.0
RELEASE_ID=6.4.0-hyp3r.13
BASE_IMAGE=swift:6.4.0-noble
BASE_IMAGE_SLIM=swift:6.4.0-noble-slim
LIBDISPATCH_REPO=Hyp3rSon1X/swift-corelibs-libdispatch
LIBDISPATCH_REF=c28dbc510e6330f15542343e6bbb88037a97d815
FOUNDATION_REPO=Hyp3rSon1X/swift-corelibs-foundation
FOUNDATION_REF=2eb0e1f820d59fb1f7622a564cfb83c9d01b6b14
SWIFT_FOUNDATION_TAG=swift-6.4.0-RELEASE
SWIFT_FOUNDATION_ICU_TAG=swift-6.4.0-RELEASE
SWIFT_COLLECTIONS_TAG=1.1.6
FIXES="SC-0001: libdispatch use-after-free in the Linux epoll backend, SIGSEGV in _dispatch_event_loop_drain (swiftlang/swift-corelibs-libdispatch#949); backport of upstream PR #965 onto swift-6.4.0-RELEASE. SC-0002: Foundation Process on Linux over-reads dirent.d_name in findMaximumOpenFromProcSelfFD, intermittent SIGSEGV (swiftlang/swift-corelibs-foundation#5472); backport of upstream commit 81eb85a2 onto swift-6.4.0-RELEASE. SC-0004: the optimizer moved a class field-offset load above the allocation of the first instance (metadata accessors are modelled as readnone), so the first object of a class with a non-constant layout could get a field store over its isa pointer, intermittent SIGSEGV or silent heap corruption in -O builds; fixed in swift-frontend (LLVM alias analysis of swift_allocObject), the Linux images and tarballs carry the rebuilt compiler SC-0006: #isolation in nonisolated(nonsending) code (the default under NonisolatedNonsendingByDefault) ignored its contextual type, e.g. #isolation === MainActor.shared, so -O builds aborted in the LLVM verifier ('PHINode should have one entry for each predecessor', swiftlang/swift#92798); now converted, and types (any Actor)? cannot convert to are diagnosed like in @MainActor code (#isolation != nil there becomes an error; write (#isolation as (any Actor)?) != nil). SC-0019: #isolation in nonisolated(nonsending) code was consumed without a copy, so e.g. String(describing: #isolation) over-released the calling actor (deinit while running, then SIGSEGV; swiftlang/swift#92799). Both fixed in swift-frontend; the Linux images and tarballs carry the rebuilt compiler. SC-0005: a typed-throws closure passed to a generic untyped-throws parameter (e.g. Task { () async throws(E) -> T in ... }) crashed the compiler for error types with storage and returned a corrupted error for small enums (swiftlang/swift#92312, a 6.4 regression); fixed in swift-frontend. SC-0003: -O builds of async functions that take a small enum or struct whose native explosion is coerced through a stack temporary (e.g. an enum with a tuple payload) could lose their spilled self and arguments: IRGen sized the temporary's lifetime markers in bits instead of bytes, so after the temporary moved into the async frame the optimizer deleted the spills, and the first resume read garbage (SIGSEGV or wrong values); backport of upstream swiftlang/swift#91312 (main only), fixed in swift-frontend. SC-0022: a typed-throws closure whose context type is a type parameter (stored in [() throws(E) -> T], passed through a generic id<T>) crashed the compiler in SILGen; fixed in swift-frontend."
# Patched Static Linux SDK (musl): the official bundle below with libdispatch.a and libFoundation.a rebuilt from the refs above.
STATIC_SDK_VERSION=0.1.0
STATIC_SDK_URL=https://download.swift.org/swift-6.4.0-release/static-sdk/swift-6.4.0-RELEASE/swift-6.4.0-RELEASE_static-linux-0.1.0.artifactbundle.tar.gz
STATIC_SDK_SHA256=47d2fd89eebfdf9eb4d536b6710414297f755c17926cdebc4742c08982b40a9e
# Compiler overlay (SC-0003, SC-0004, SC-0005, SC-0006, SC-0019, SC-0022): swift-frontend rebuilt from the ref below plus the unmodified swift-6.4.0-RELEASE
# LLVM/Clang/cmark/swift-syntax/string-processing trees, release build without assertions, swapped into the official toolchain.
# The static SDK's own libraries do not depend on the compiler fix; code built against it still uses the host compiler.
SWIFT_REPO=Hyp3rSon1X/swift
SWIFT_REF=156f937bba13cb543b8747ed12429978199e82ad
SWIFT_UPSTREAM_TAG=swift-6.4.0-RELEASE
